 "problems": [
  "No report or notes file existed for am-02; an earlier run had written 9 dossiers (mayan-city-states, later-mayan-city-states, itza-mayans, tikal, calakmul, caracol, copan, palenque, dos-pilas). All validate and were kept unchanged; they are counted with 'kept from an earlier run' in the name field and tikal, calakmul, caracol, copan, palenque, dos-pilas are listed under new_slugs.",
  "mayapan.json and k-iche-kingdom.json had their identity.successors extended by a small direct JSON edit after the builder script (provinces added as successors; kaqchikel-kingdom added to the K'iche' successors); both still validate.",
  "Counterpart strings differ across dossiers: copan uses 'Quirigua', calakmul and caracol use 'Naranjo', tikal uses 'Uaxactun'; slugs 'quirigua' and 'naranjo' now exist. The colour/ledger agents should normalise them.",
  "Two Cliopatria rows share Wikidata Q28567 (Mayan City-States, Later Mayan City-States); kept as two dossiers because the shapes are different northern/southern envelopes. The orchestrator may merge them.",
  "Cliopatria's Later Mayan City-States stays to 1546 and Itza Mayans to 1699 while the dossiers end the provinces 1529-1547 and the Itza in March 1697.",
  "Most province pages (Sotuta, Cupul, Chikinchel, Tases) are stubs; the provinces are discs around capitals, soft; four capital points and Piedras Negras are the researcher's geographic knowledge, flagged in each dossier.",
  "The earlier run's keyframes say a 20 km disc is 'the grid's minimum'; a 10 km radius already resolves to one 253 km2 cell. New dossiers use nominal sizes and say so.",
  "WebFetch answers were summarised by a small model; quotes in notes are those it returned (all under its 125-character limit), not full sentences."
 ]
}